  "caveats": [
    "The source normalization assumes five-slot interior groups; several poorly printed erasure runs on A3 do not reveal exact placement independently. Those assumptions are retained in each source record.",
    "Raw A5 has177source slots, an odd total. Ordinary complete ADFGVX requires an even number. The176-slot model is inherited from prior art and is explicitly conditional.",
    "A3 comment42 fills63erased coordinates and changes five known ones. A5 comment41 fills25erased coordinates and changes two known ones in addition to its length repair. These are not new observations.",
    "Nov7-9 square cells for digits5and6 are unassigned. The audit enumerates both globally consistent assignments and reports their union; it never assigns the digit independently at each occurrence.",
    "The new A4 sibling and C1 contextual helper have direct readable fragments but retain source garbles. They do not uniquely supply the erased positions of A3 or A5.",
    "C1 is an earlier five-part UKS transmission on the same date, and its evening report concerns the Danube crossing at Belgrade. Its identity with the A3-A5 multipart message remains a hypothesis.",
    "The printedp163eighteen-part message is separate and cannot be silently used as the missing first two parts."
  ]
